A roulette wheel has the numbers $0, 1, 2, \ldots, 36$ where each of the 37 numbers is equally likely to be spun.

\exfigure{5832_q20_1}

If the wheel is spun $18\,500$ times, calculate the expected frequency of spinning the number 8.

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{5832_q25_s1}

The colours are the same if both apples are red or both are green.
$$\begin{aligned} P(\text{same colour}) &= P(RR)+P(GG) \\ &= \dfrac{9}{17}\times\dfrac{8}{16}+\dfrac{8}{17}\times\dfrac{7}{16} \\ &= \dfrac{8}{17} \end{aligned}$$

